Negative control for the row action's outcome feedback (P1-R13).

Fires the live action directly, bypassing `useActionFeedback` — so a mutation
that succeeds says nothing and one that fails says nothing either, which is the
fire-and-forget defect the operator drove into ("none of the actions actually
work").

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: list-surface-action-feedback.spec.ts — the success-toast and
failure-toast cases.

